{number: 163}
{title: Sun of My Soul}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Sun of my soul, Thou [F] Savior [C] dear,
It is not night if [G7] Thou be [C] near;
O may no earthborn [F] cloud a-[C] rise
To hide Thee from Thy [G7] servant's [C] eyes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [C] the soft dews of [F] kindly [C] sleep
My wearied eyelids [G7] gently [C] steep,
Be my last thought, how [F] sweet to [C] rest
Forever on my [G7] Savior's [C] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
A-[C] bide with me from [F] morn till [C] eve,
For without Thee I [G7] cannot [C] live;
Abide with me when [F] night is [C] nigh,
For without Thee I [G7] dare not [C] die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Come [C] near and bless us [F] when we [C] wake,
Ere through the world our [G7] way we [C] take,
Till in the ocean [F] of Thy [C] love
We lose ourselves in [G7] heaven a-[C] bove.
{end_of_verse}
